// ---- Patch notes (newest first). Every update to the game adds an entry here and bumps SQ_VERSION. ----
const PATCH_NOTES=[
 {v:'2026.11.13-18',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'New shops, quests and treasure on the islands (coming soon)',n:['The islands are getting busier: islanders can now run their own shops and hand out quests. Talk to them to see what they sell or need; their quests show up in your quest log with the reward.','Some new items, recipes, monsters and loot will start appearing over the next updates.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-17',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Developer gifts, announcements and XP events',n:['Gifts from the developer: if something went wrong (a lost item, a bug), you can now be sent items, gold and a note. They land in your bag the next time you play, or right away if you\'re on.','Replies to your bug reports now reach you in the game.','Announcements show as a banner at the top of the screen. Tap × to close it.','XP events (like Double XP weekends): while one runs, a small purple tag in the top corner shows how long is left, and all XP you earn is multiplied.','World Market: fixed a way to put items and gold into the collection box that hadn\'t really been traded. Filled offers now stay up a few seconds longer behind the scenes so every sale is paid out.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-16',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Pick your ultimate, and smoother controllers in chests',n:['Pick your ultimate: if your gear gives more than one (a Stone Sledgehammer, a wand, the Dragonsoul amulet), choose which one the ULT button uses in the Gear tab, under ULTIMATE.','Controllers: in a chest or bag, the d-pad now reaches every button on an item card (including the wide "Take all"/"Put in all" button), and ○ closes the card with the highlight back on the same item instead of jumping to the first one.','Monsters that shoot can now have their own look, attack speed, extra damage and status effects (slowed, burning, frozen or poisoned) set by the developer, so watch out for new tricks.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-15',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Fixes from your bug reports',n:['Fixed: furniture placed in front of a house\'s back door could trap you when you came back in from the backyard. That spot is now kept clear, anything already there is moved aside, and if you ever end up inside furniture you step out of it.','Fixed: the general store showed "undefined" next to some items you could sell.','Fixed: the crafting screen showed "Sword: undefined" while holding the Crystal Sword.','Phones now stay awake while you play, so the screen no longer dims and locks while you fish or cook.','During an island boss fight the world boss banner gets out of the way, so you can see the island boss\'s health bar.','World bosses on the other islands now always appear on open ground you can walk to (the Ancient Dragon could end up over spots you couldn\'t reach).']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-14',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Beetles come back up, and no more top price on the World Market',n:['Fixed: beetles that burrowed into the ground never came back out (they got stuck out of sight). Now they burst out of the sand next to you again, everywhere they live.','World Market: there is no maximum price any more. Ask whatever you think something is worth; if it\'s too much, nobody will buy it. The minimum price stays.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-13',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'No more surprise trips back to spawn',n:['Fixed: logging in could put you back at the spawn point (for example after fishing on Gull Rock). It happened when you had saved standing where a rock or tree used to be and it had grown back. Now you\'re placed right next to where you left off.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-12',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'A brand-new orchestral soundtrack',n:['All new music: 18 original songs played on real orchestral instruments (flutes, strings, harp, horns, choir, accordion and more) in a concert-hall sound.','Every island has its own theme now: Briarwood, Ashfall Coast, Ironcrest Highlands, the Shattered Expanse and No Man\'s Land.','New sailing song for the open sea, and boss music that starts when a boss is near (island bosses, world bosses, dungeon bosses and Dev Suite bosses).','Hollow by day and night, houses, Saltmere, Frosthollow, Tidewatch, Dusthaven, the caves and every dungeon got new songs, and the loops are much longer.','The instruments load the first time a song plays, so a new area\'s song can take a moment to start. Music volume and the on/off switch in Options work as before.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-11',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'PvP rebalance: fights that end',n:['Your gear and levels now count against other players: hits do 1 to 3 hearts depending on your weapon, combat level and perks (the same numbers as against monsters). Ultimates hit harder still.','Heavy armour (mostly mithril or better) takes 1 off big hits from players.','After a player hits you, you can be hit again sooner (half a second instead of a full second), so landing hits in a row pays off.','Blocking stops at most 1 in 4 player attacks. Against monsters it works as before.','While fighting a player (a duel, or PvP damage in the last 10 seconds), food and other healing work at half strength and you can eat every 5 seconds instead of 3. Against monsters nothing changes.','Duels: after 1 minute it\'s SUDDEN DEATH, and nobody can heal any more. The duel bar shows it.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-10',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Fixes from a full check-up',n:['Fixed: the Safe Haven and Sacred Flames campfire perks did nothing. Now monsters at the edge of your campfire\'s light hold back (Safe Haven), and monsters near a campfire move more slowly (Sacred Flames).','Sound: music and rain no longer keep playing in stuttering bits when you switch to another tab or app; they pause and come back when you return.','Sound: pressing a key now starts the music too, not just a click or tap.','Backyards and courtyards play the outdoor day and night music instead of the house tune.','Behind the scenes: a link-opening problem that once broke the Discord button is fixed for good, and the game saves a little less often for no reason.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-9',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Seeds, pets and controller fixes',n:['Farming: the higher your level, the more seeds your harvests give. Every 10 levels adds a 5% chance of a second seed, and the Farming skill tree now shows your seed chances at every level.','Three new Farming perks (a third choice at levels 20, 40 and 70): Seed Pouch (seeds 15% more often), Twin Seeds (each seed can come as two) and Heirloom Seeds (at least one seed from every harvest).','Fixed: the Mushling and Glowcap pets showed an empty PET slot even when you had one out. They now show in the slot, and a spare one in your bag is saved properly.','Controllers: an item card in a chest (the one that asks how many to move) can now be closed with ○, and the highlight stays inside the card while it\'s open. ○ again closes the chest.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-8',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Controllers everywhere, deposit bag',n:['Controller players can now answer trade, party and duel requests: after a moment the request is highlighted, ✕ picks TRADE (or JOIN, DUEL, PLAY) and ○ says no. The update bar works the same way.','Controllers reach every part of every menu, including text boxes, dropdowns and checkboxes.','New on-screen keyboard for controllers, like the one in Pokemon: pick a text box and press ✕. ✕ types, ○ deletes, △ adds a space, □ switches capitals, R1 shows symbols and Options (START) is OK. In chat, OK sends your message.','HIT no longer tills or waters on any device: the hoe and watering can are off-hand tools. Use X or right-click on a computer, R1 on a controller, or the new TILL / WATER button on touch screens.','Chests have a DEPOSIT BAG button that puts everything in your bag into the chest at once.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-7',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Home comforts',n:['Light campfires in your backyard or courtyard (FIRE, 3 wood and a stone, like anywhere outdoors). Cook at them, warm up, and they keep burning there while you\'re inside.','No more getting hungry at home: your food doesn\'t go down while you\'re inside your house or castle. Sleeping in your bed still uses up some food overnight.','Wardrobes can now be picked up: open the wardrobe and tap PICK UP WARDROBE at the bottom.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-6',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'One save: your Google account',n:['You now sign in with Google to play. Your character lives in your Google account, so it\'s the same on your phone, your computer and the Windows app.','Only one device or tab can play your account at a time. Open the game somewhere else and the old one stops with a PLAY HERE INSTEAD button; tap it to take your game back with your latest progress.','No more "Which save do you want?" questions. The first time you sign in after this update, the game keeps whichever save has more progress (this device\'s or your account\'s) and backs up the other one in Options > Backups.','If your connection drops, you\'ll see "Not saved: reconnecting..." at the top. Your progress saves again as soon as you\'re back online.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-5',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Placing your castle',n:['Fixed: after packing up your house, the game could still say "You already have a house" and refuse to place your castle (or a new house) while other players\' houses were nearby. Only your own home counts now.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-4',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Living backyards',n:['The trees, bushes and ponds in backyards and courtyards now work like everywhere else: chop the trees for logs (oak and maple too, with the right axe), pick berries and hazelnuts from the bushes, and fish in the pond with your rod.','What you take grows back after a few minutes. While it regrows, you can\'t plant or build on that spot.','Visiting a friend\'s yard? You can fish in their pond, but their trees and bushes are theirs.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-3',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Warlord\'s blade fix',n:['Fixed: a Warlord\'s blade in your hand turned into a steel sword when you loaded your game. The same happened to mithril and adamant axes and pickaxes. They now stay what they are.','If this happened to you, your lost Warlord\'s blade, axe or pickaxe is back in your Bag the next time you play (as long as you don\'t still have one somewhere). Sorry about that!']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-2',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'Bigger, prettier backyards and courtyards',n:['Courtyards are much bigger now: a stone terrace below your castle, wide paths, a pond in a paved plaza, an avenue of trees and orchards in the corners, with plenty of open lawn for farming and furniture.','Backyards are bigger too, with a path, a little patio, a pond and trees.','Both now sit in a clearing in the forest with soft grass and wildflowers, and your own house or castle stands behind you. No more odd edges or dark gaps around them.','Only grass can be tilled: the stone paths and patios stay clear.','Walk up the path into the door to go back inside. Going through a door no longer bounces you straight back if you keep holding the button.','Everything you already placed or planted came along. Anything that ended up on a tree, the pond or the path to the door moved to the nearest free spot.']},
 {v:'2026.11.13-1',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:'More room for new content',n:['Behind the scenes: island bosses, world bosses and the Imp can now get fresh looks, monsters can get tougher (or gentler) hits, and the islands can get new caves, monster grounds and paths. Watch for changes as they arrive!']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-20',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Backyards, courtyards and a royal throne',n:['Backyards: every house now has a back door in the middle of its back wall. It leads to your own private backyard, a fenced lawn where you can place furniture and farm in peace: till with your hoe, plant seeds from your Bag, water and harvest like anywhere else.','Castles get two back gates beside the throne that open onto a courtyard: bigger and grander, with stone paths, flower beds and a fountain.','Only friends you trust can step into your backyard or courtyard. They can look around but can\'t change anything.','One home each: you can now have one house or one castle in the world. If you had more, you keep one (a castle first) and the others were packed into your bag with all their furniture and everything in their chests.','Castle halls are now perfectly symmetrical: the gate and the red carpet line up with the throne. Nothing you placed inside was moved or lost.','A brand new throne: gold and red velvet on a stone dais.','Dungeon bosses can now get new looks and new drops from the game\'s artists, and new bosses can appear on the islands.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-19',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Melee stays melee on PC',n:['Keyboard and mouse: Space and left-click now only use your main hand. They no longer shoot your bow or till and water with your hoe or watering can. Use X or right-click for your off-hand.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-18',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Messages at the top on phones',n:['On phones held upright, the message box now sits in the strip at the very top of the screen instead of the middle, so it no longer covers you or what you\'re doing. Tap it to skip ahead like before.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-17',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Weekly events, chess ladder, party perks',n:['Weekly events: every week the whole server works on one goal together, like chopping 3,000 logs or lighting 300 fires. Find it in your quest log, under the daily challenges. When the community reaches a tier, everyone who helped gets gold and XP. A new event starts every Monday.','Chess ladder: games of chess against other players now give you a rating (everyone starts at 1000). Beat stronger players to climb faster. See the top players in Leaderboards > Chess, and your own rating at Orla\'s board. Very short games and more than 3 games a day against the same player aren\'t rated.','Parties: the chat has a new Party tab for talking to your party. When you beat a monster, party members nearby get half its gold too.','The watering can is now an off-hand item, like the hoe. Farming swaps them for you: HIT dry crops with the hoe in hand and you switch to the can, HIT grass with the can and you switch to the hoe.','Controllers: R1 now uses a hoe or watering can in your off-hand too, not just a bow or wand.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-16',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Graves outside dungeons',n:['Fall in a dungeon, an island boss lair or another building and your grave now appears just outside its entrance, so you can always get your things back, even without shards or sigils to open the door again.','Graves that were already inside a dungeon or lair also show up outside the entrance now.','Your grave timer says "(outside)" when that\'s where it is, and the map shows the spot.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-15',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Skill perks that do what they say',n:['Flame Aura now works: you glow at night and in dark caves, with no campfire needed. Other players see your glow too.','Speed perks for Cooking, Firemaking, Smithing and Crafting (and the speed you gain from levels) now really make those actions faster. Before, they quietly gave a little extra XP, from back when those actions were instant.','Safe Haven and Sacred Flames now work on every monster near your campfire, not just slimes.','Golden Forge now raises the price of everything you smelt or forge, Golden Goods covers everything you build, and Golden Touch covers gold, mithril and adamant ore too.','A few perks got clearer names and descriptions (Charcoal Bed, Farmhand\'s Stamina, Careful Cutting).']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-14',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Mithril and adamant tools',n:['Forge mithril and adamant axes and pickaxes at an anvil: 2 bars and a log each (Smithing 52 for mithril, 67 for adamant).','They hit much harder than steel, so trees and rocks come down in fewer swings. A mithril tool needs Woodcutting or Mining 30, an adamant one 45.','The Woodcutting, Mining and Smithing skill trees now show these levels. The Smithing tree also lists everything else the anvil makes, including mithril and adamant gear and bows, which were missing.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-13',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Off-hand key, hoe in the off-hand',n:['Keyboard and mouse: press X to use your off-hand. With a bow or wand it shoots or casts toward your mouse pointer (hold to keep firing); with the hoe it tills the ground in front of you. Right-click still works, and you can change the key in Options > Controls.','The hoe is now an off-hand item, so there\'s no separate HOE slot any more. Equip it in place of your bow or wand to farm. If you had both, your hoe is waiting in your bag.','The players-online count now sits right above the day box.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-12',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'World bosses on the map, players online, fewer pop-ups',n:['World bosses now show on the map: a red ring with the boss\'s icon on the world map (with its name and time left), on the island map and on your minimap, right where it is. The map also says which island it\'s on.','Far fewer pop-up boxes: most short messages now float over your head instead. The big box is kept for quests, level-ups, rare finds and people talking to you.','The top corner of your minimap now shows how many players are online, next to a green dot.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-11',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Tidier screen',n:['Eating ("Ate cooked meat") no longer opens the big text box: it floats over your head.','XP and food numbers over your head are smaller.','On phones, your party list now sits on the left under the quest box instead of covering the CHAT button.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-10',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Emotes you act out',n:['Emotes are now acted out by your character instead of a bubble: wave your arm, bow, dance (spinning and hopping), cheer with both arms up and confetti, laugh, send hearts, nod yes, shake your head no, think, sit down or fall asleep. Everyone nearby sees it.','New emotes: Sit and Sleep (they last until you move). Walking ends any emote.','Find them in START > Emotes, press G on a keyboard, or type /wave, /dance, /cheer, /sit and so on in chat.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-9',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Quieter skilling',n:['"Reeling it in...", "Cooking...", "Smelting..." and the like no longer pop up in the big text box: your character already shows what you\'re doing.','Small messages like "It got away..." are now smaller and follow you.','Fixed: dungeon boss quests in the quest tracker said things like "Defeat the Dunes" instead of the boss\'s name (now "Defeat the Sandclaw Matriarch").','The USE button\'s word (SAIL, OPEN, SLEEP...) no longer flips back to USE now and then.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-8',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Discord button fixed',n:['Fixed: the JOIN OUR DISCORD button on the title screen didn\'t open anything. It now opens our Discord invite on phones, computers and the Windows app.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-7',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Chess with friends, parties and emotes',n:['Play chess with other players: tap someone\'s name and choose CHESS. You can both stake items and gold, like a duel, and the winner takes both stakes. Games against players give no Tactics XP. A move can take up to 3 minutes.','Grandmaster Orla is much easier to beat now, especially on Novice and Club player. Resigning straight away, or resigning game after game, no longer gives Tactics XP.','Opening Moves is now Orla\'s own side quest instead of part of Elder Rowan\'s story. If you were on it, it\'s waiting for you at her table.','You can\'t be hurt while you\'re playing chess.','Parties: tap a player\'s name and choose INVITE TO PARTY (up to 4 players). Party members show in green on the map and minimap, with their health under the minimap and a star over their heads. You get +10% XP while one is close by, and /p in chat talks to your party. START > Party lists everyone.','Emotes: START > Emotes (G on a keyboard), or type /wave, /dance, /cheer, /love, /bow, /laugh, /yes, /no in chat. Everyone nearby sees them.','Voyages now come from one person: Sera, the Navigator in Tidewatch. Take on every voyage and report back to her. Harbor posts still list the sea routes and sell boat upgrades.','Hollow Island now has open sea all the way around its edge. Anything you built where the land became sea is safe in your bag.','Your houses and castles show on the map and minimap, and so do other players\' houses on Hollow.','Join the SkillQuest Discord: there\'s a JOIN OUR DISCORD button on the title screen.','Smith your own tools: iron and steel axes and pickaxes at the anvil. You can craft a fishing rod in the Craft menu, and the general store now buys everything you build or craft.','Duel wins now count as PvP kills on the leaderboard. Falling no longer resets your Monsters count, and the Quests board counts every quest you\'ve finished (village quests, voyages and Orla\'s too).','Small messages like "You cast your line" now float over your head instead of opening the big text box. On phones, a world boss somewhere else shows as a small chip; the full banner appears when you reach the fight.','Fixed: the TALK/USE button flickering next to harbor posts, furnaces, anvils and chests. XP numbers now show over your head on every island, in dungeons and indoors.','Fixed: you could cook on a castle as if it were a campfire (its warmth still heals you and keeps monsters away). Boats can no longer ride up onto bridges and piers.','Fixed: item descriptions showing their stats twice. Dungeon monsters (like Scorpion Hollow\'s dust skeletons) now use their own looks, and the wiki shows monster changes right away.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-6',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Achievements, collection log and duels',n:['Achievements: START > Achievements. Over 40 goals across skills, gathering, combat, quests, travel, wealth and collecting. Each one pays gold the moment you reach it.','Collection log: the second page of Achievements shows every item, piece of gear and pet in the game. What you\'ve had shows in colour; the rest is a mystery shape until you find it.','Players: stand next to someone and the TALK button shows their name. Tap it for TRADE, ADD FRIEND and DUEL (chess is coming).','Duels: challenge someone, then both put in a stake of items and gold and accept twice. Fight anywhere, PvP on or off. The duel ends when one of you falls: you get back up right where you fell, and the winner takes the loser\'s stake (and keeps their own). Leaving the area or going offline loses the duel; after 3 minutes it\'s a draw and both stakes go back.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-5',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Elder Rowan\'s second chapter',n:['The story goes on! After Three Villages, One Island, Elder Rowan sends you across the sea: sail to Briarwood Isle, help Thornbrook, brave the Ashfall Coast, and open an island\'s sealed door to face its boss.','The new finale, Legend of the Isles: defeat all five island bosses for 5,000 gold. Grandmaster now asks for total level 150 and pays 1,500 gold.','The quest box tells you how to get there: which voyage to take, which boat upgrade you need, and which village quest is next.','Fixes: Slime Trouble and Slime Slayer now count slimes only. Night Watch is a real challenge: see one whole night through, dusk to dawn, without falling.','No more doing the same job twice: Northern Supplies now wants oak logs, The Ranger\'s Warning wolf pelts, and Across the Western Sea cooked salmon.','The Road East (a short walk to Saltmere) now comes early, right after Gone Fishing. Your progress is kept: anything you already finished stays finished.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-4',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Smooth camera',n:['No more shaky screen: your character used to jump a little back and forth while walking, especially on phones. You now stay perfectly still in the middle of the screen.','The world also scrolls smoothly now instead of in small jumps, so walking, sprinting and sailing look much steadier.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-3',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Check for updates and move your buttons',n:['Phones and tablets: move the touch buttons where your thumbs like them. Options > Controls > Touch > Move my buttons, then drag HIT, EAT, FIRE, TALK, ROLL, ULT and BOW/CAST anywhere, and make any of them bigger or smaller. Portrait and landscape each keep their own layout.','No more refreshing to get the newest version: Options > Check for updates. If there\'s a new version, UPDATE NOW saves your game and loads it.','The game also checks by itself every 10 minutes and shows an "Update ready" bar at the top. Tap UPDATE when it suits you, or LATER to keep playing.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-2',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'Your own controls',n:['Change your keys and controller buttons: Options > Controls. Pick an action, tap Change, then press the new key or button. Taking one another action uses swaps the two.','Keyboard: every action can move, including walking, sprinting, hitting, eating, the campfire, talking, rolling, the ultimate and the bag, map, quests, skills and craft screens. The middle and side mouse buttons can be used too.','Controller: hit, talk/use, roll, eat, campfire, bow/wand, L1, quests, sprint, bag and map can all go on the buttons you like. Menus keep ✕ to pick and ○ to go back.','Your layout is kept on each device, and Reset puts the original back. The button hints and the help box show your keys.']},
 {v:'2026.11.12-1',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:'HIT does what you meant',n:['Your weapon in hand now looks just like it does in your bag: swords, the sledgehammer, axes, pickaxes, wands and bows are drawn with their own item picture as you swing, chop, mine, cast and shoot. Other players see your sword swings the same way.','Chopping and mining now show just your axe or pickaxe swing, never the sword swing on top of it. This works for every kind of tree, ore and boulder, on every island and in dungeons too, and other players see it the same way.','HIT no longer casts spells. With a wand it used to fire a spell whenever a monster was somewhere ahead, even while you were chopping a tree. Use the CAST button (or the mouse on a computer) to cast.','Casting a spell no longer flashes a sword swing at the end.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-14',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Quest tracking and chat',n:['Three Villages, One Island now tells you exactly what\'s next: the quest box names the village and the next step there (for example "Dusthaven: talk to Zahra"), and the arrow points the way. Its card in the quest log lists how far you are in each village.','You can stop tracking quests: open the quest log, tap the tracked quest and tap "Tracking · tap to stop". The quest box disappears until you track a quest again.','On phones and tablets the chat window now opens at the bottom of the screen and moves up above the keyboard while you type. The CHAT button stays where it was.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-13',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Daily challenges and a TRADE button',n:['Daily challenges: every day you get three small tasks, such as chop 30 logs, catch 10 fish or beat 12 monsters. They\'re at the top of your quest log (tap the quest box).','Each finished challenge pays gold and XP in that skill right away. Finish all three for a streak bonus that grows every day in a row, up to 7 days. New challenges arrive at midnight.','Only what you gather, make or beat yourself counts. Things you buy or get in a trade don\'t.','Trading is quicker: stand right next to another player and the TALK button says TRADE. One tap asks them, and if they already asked you, the same tap says yes. When you both have PvP on, the button stays out of the way so it never gets in the way of a fight (START > Trade still works).']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-12',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Buttons say what they do',n:['The action buttons now name what they\'ll do right now: CHOP at a tree, MINE at a rock or ore, PICK at a bush or mushroom patch, FISH at the water and REEL while your line is out.','At a furnace, anvil, stove or crafting bench the button says SMELT, SMITH, COOK or CRAFT. At a chest it says OPEN, at a bed SLEEP, and at a sign READ.','Standing at a fire with something to cook, EAT turns into COOK.','The TALK button says OPEN, SLEEP, READ or ENTER (or the station\'s job) instead of USE.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-11',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: monster editor',n:['The developer can now redraw monsters and tune how tough they are, how fast they move and what they drop. Nothing changes in your game yet; changes will arrive in later updates.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-10',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: testing tools',n:['The developer has new tools for checking updates in the game quickly, so new things can be tried out before they reach you.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-9',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: redrawing more of the world',n:['The developer can now also redraw everything you build (workstations, furniture, chests, beds, campfires, fences, walls and gates), farm soil and crops at every stage, boats, things inside shops, homes, dungeons and caves, and the island villages.','Props can have their own look at night, like a lamp that glows after dark.','Chopped trees, mined rocks and picked plants can leave something behind while they grow back.','Nothing changes in your game yet; new looks will arrive in later updates.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-8',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: redrawing the world',n:['The developer can now give trees, rocks, ores, mushrooms, cacti, bushes, town buildings, houses, street lamps, wells, signposts, bridges, tall grass and island props a new look, and even animate them. Nothing changes in your game yet; new looks will arrive in later updates.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-7',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Islands with people, dungeons and monsters',n:['New islands can now have people to talk to: walk up to them and press TALK, and they tell you something new each time.','New islands can have their own dungeons. Walk up into the cave opening to go down, and walk back out to return to the island.','Monsters now live in set areas on new islands, so you know where the fights are. Beaten monsters come back after a while.','New islands can have their own ground art and their own place on the sea chart.','Fixed: monsters didn\'t appear on new islands that were meant to have them.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-6',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Fairer World Market',n:['Up to 2 offers per item (still 8 offers in total), so one player can\'t fill the whole list for an item.','Prices must be within a sensible range for each item, from half its shop value up to 25 times it (at least 100 gold). The range is shown when you make an offer.','A price far from the usual one shows a warning and needs a second tap, so an extra zero can\'t slip through.','Offers now last 7 days. After that, whatever hasn\'t traded comes back to you on its own. My offers shows how long each one has left. Offers that are already up get the full 7 days, starting tomorrow.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-5',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Pets that help',n:['Treelings now help you chop: while one follows you, every tree you chop has a chance to give an extra log. Rarer treelings are better at it (from 10% for a Treeling up to 22% for a Void treeling), and each one is twice as good on its own kind of tree.','New pet: the Mushling, a little red mushroom (1 in 1,000 when picking mushroom patches). When you\'re hurt it puffs healing spores at you now and then (+1 heart); when you\'re fine, it brings you mushrooms.','New pet: the Glowcap, a glowing blue mushroom (1 in 2,500 from mushroom patches). When something hits you it can burst into spores that slow every monster around you.','Both new pets are in the wiki\'s rare drops, and you can switch pets under START > Style.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-4',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Smithing, smelting and crafting come alive',n:['At the anvil you raise your hammer and ring it down on red-hot metal, with sparks on every blow.','At the furnace you hold a crucible to the fire and pour glowing metal into a mould.','Crafting: you saw and shape the piece in front of you while shavings fall.','Other players nearby see and hear all of it too.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-3',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'A friendlier start',n:['New players get a short Getting started guide in the quest box: talk to the Elder, chop wood by hand, make an axe and a pickaxe, mine stone and light a first campfire.','Each step says exactly which button to press, an arrow points to the nearest tree, rock or the Elder, and the button you need glows.','Stuck? After a little while a hint pops up to help.','Every step pays a small reward straight away, with a warm meal at the end.','Tap the quest box any time to open your quest log. You can skip the guide from there.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-2',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Item cards in chests',n:['Tapping an item while looking in a chest now opens its card: what it is, its stats, how many are in the chest and in your bag, and what it sells for.','Choose how many to move: 1, 5, 10, half, all, or type any amount.','Works in your friends\' chests too.']},
 {v:'2026.11.11-1',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:'Fight island bosses together',n:['Island bosses can now be fought together online. Open the sealed door (five shards each) while a friend is already inside, and you join their fight instead of starting your own.','The boss picks a new target every few seconds, so everyone in the arena has to dodge. You see every attack aimed at your friends, too.','The boss gets more health for each extra fighter.','Everyone in the arena when the boss falls gets the full reward, and rolls for the rare drop on their own.','If the player who opened the door leaves or falls, the fight carries on for whoever is still inside.']},
 {v:'2026.11.10-4',d:'Nov 10, 2026',t:'Correct online count',n:['Fixed: right after loading in, the online count (and the player list) showed players who had already left. It now only counts who is really here.']},
 {v:'2026.11.10-3',d:'Nov 10, 2026',t:'Fishing, firemaking and cooking look alive',n:['No more progress bar over your head: your character shows the work instead.','Fishing: a proper cast over your shoulder, a float that bobs and ripples, a splash when something bites, a bending rod while you reel it in, and your catch flying out of the water to you.','Lighting a fire: you crouch at a little pile of kindling and strike flint and steel until the sparks catch.','Cooking: you crouch by the fire turning your food on a stick as it browns and steams.','Other players now see you fishing, lighting fires and cooking too.']},
 {v:'2026.11.10-2',d:'Nov 10, 2026',t:'The sledgehammer smashes ore',n:['The Stone Sledgehammer now breaks any rock or ore vein in one hit (you still need the Mining level and pickaxe for it).','GROUND SLAM now also smashes every rock, ore vein, boulder and ore boulder around you that you could mine, and you get everything inside.','Other players now see your GROUND SLAM: the shockwave, the dust and the sound.']},
 {v:'2026.11.10-1',d:'Nov 10, 2026',t:'Livelier pets',n:['Pets with a new look can now have two standing frames they idle between and two walking frames they step between.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-10',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'Redesigned gear shows for everyone',n:['Fixed: when a piece of gear had a new look, other players saw you without it (a redesigned helmet looked like no helmet at all). Everyone now sees the new look. If their game hasn\'t loaded it yet, they see the old look instead.','When a piece of armour gets a new look, your outfit dye still recolours it, keeping its light and dark shading.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-9',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: gear art tools',n:['The developer\'s gear editor now shows the character exactly as the game draws it, so new looks for armour and weapons fit properly. Nothing changes in your game.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-8',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'New gear and special effects between updates',n:['Brand-new weapons and armour can now arrive without a full update. Look for them in island treasure chests and at the anvil.','Gear can now have special effects while you wear it: life steal, setting enemies on fire, slowing them, critical hits, faster walking and bonus XP. Effects from every piece you wear add up.','Weapon and armour numbers (damage, bow range, block chance, a wand\'s mana cost) and what each piece needs can now be tuned too. Descriptions always show the numbers that really apply.','Your saves are untouched, and new gear you own is kept safe even if it takes a moment to load.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-7',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'New looks for pets',n:['Pets can now get brand new looks. When one does, everyone sees it on everyone\'s pet. Pets without a new look stay exactly as they are.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-6',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'Treasure on new islands',n:['New islands can now have buildings, signs to read and treasure chests. Find a chest, press USE and the treasure is yours: each chest can be opened once by every player.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-5',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'World Market trades, stoves and chests fixed',n:['Fixed: buying or selling at the World Market against someone else\'s offer always failed with "The market couldn\'t take that offer". Offers now trade straight away, and a buy and sell offer that match will also find each other on their own a moment later.','Fixed: cooking at a stove did nothing since the last big update. "Cook all" works again.','Fixed: stoves, furnaces, anvils and crafting benches use the materials in nearby chests again (or every chest in the house), not just what\'s in your bag.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-4',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'New islands on the horizon',n:['New hand-built islands can now appear on the sailing routes. When one does, sail to it from any harbor post, the same as the other islands.','If an island you were standing on is ever taken off the charts, your next visit puts you safely back on Hollow Island with everything you were carrying.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-3',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'New looks for your gear',n:['Helmets, armour, legs, weapons and shields can now get their own look on your character, from the front, back and side.','Everyone sees the new looks on everyone else too, as soon as both of you have reloaded the game.','Anything that hasn\'t had a new look drawn yet looks the same as before.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-2',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'Behind the scenes: faster art and balance updates',n:['New item art and balance changes (names, prices, boss HP and rewards) can now reach you the next time you open the game, without waiting for a full update.','The game\'s code has been reorganised into smaller pieces so future updates are quicker and safer to make.','Fixed: the Options screen could fail to open for a signed-in account with no Google display name.','Nothing about how the game plays has changed, and your saves are untouched.']},
 {v:'2026.11.09-1',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:'Skilling takes time, tougher bosses, shop stock and fixes',n:['Cooking, lighting fires, smelting, smithing, crafting and reeling in fish now take 2-3 seconds each, with an animation and a progress bar over your head. "Make all" and "Cook all" make one at a time until you run out; walking away stops it.','All bosses are much tougher: island bosses have over twice the HP, world bosses twice, dungeon bosses double, and every boss hits 60% harder.','You can only eat once every 3 seconds, so you can\'t out-eat a boss\'s damage by standing still.','Shops now keep a daily stock (8 a day of ores, bars, logs and raw fish; 2 of each tool or piece of gear; 20 of everything else). What\'s left is shown on each item, and shops restock every morning.','Every bag, chest and bank slot shows the item\'s name under its picture.','Sigil shards drop twice as often (1 in 12.5).','New: skill tomes. Reading one (Bag → READ) gives XP in its skill. They can be traded and sold at the World Market.','Fixed the World Market: typing a quantity or price and then tapping SELL or BUY sometimes did nothing, and other players\' offers changing could wipe what you were typing.','Fixed trees and bushes that grew back on tilled soil not being choppable.','A world boss announcement no longer covers a message you need to read; it steps aside until the message closes.','On phones, the ONLINE/CHAT and BUG buttons now sit under the minimap instead of over the middle of the screen.']},
 {v:'2026.11.07-2',d:'Nov 7, 2026',t:'Backups on your account',n:['Backups are now kept on your account as well as on the device, so you can restore them from any device: phone, PC or the Windows app. They also survive clearing your browser.','Your account gets a backup of your save once a day when you play, and whenever a save is replaced on any device. The last 8 are kept.','Find them in Options → Backups → On your account. Tap Restore (twice) to bring one back.']},
 {v:'2026.11.07-1',d:'Nov 7, 2026',t:'Saves across devices fixed',n:['Fixed a serious bug that could lose progress when you play on more than one device: opening the game on a device with older progress could overwrite the newer progress you made on another device.','Now each device remembers which account save it last synced with. If another device has saved newer progress since, it\'s loaded automatically. If both devices have new progress, or the account save is behind this one, you choose which to keep, and the other is backed up.','New: Options → Backups lists the saves this device has backed up (whenever a save was replaced), with their total level, quest and gold. Tap Restore (twice) to bring one back. It\'s saved to your account too.','Lost progress yesterday? Open the game on the device where you had it. If it asks which save to keep, pick the one with the higher total level. If it doesn\'t ask, check Options → Backups.','Fixed Options sometimes not showing that you were signed in, so Sign out and Switch Google account were missing.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-16',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Bug fixes',n:['Fixed plateau stairways you couldn\'t walk up: about a third of them led up to the cliff edge and stopped you at the top. Every stairway now has open ground at the top and can be climbed.','Stairways no longer stop you stepping off their sides.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-15',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Tap the minimap',n:['Tap (or click) the minimap in the corner to open the full map. Works on Hollow Island, every island, and in the deep dungeons.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-14',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'SkillQuest for Windows',n:['SkillQuest is coming to Windows as its own app. On a Windows PC, Options has a Get the Windows app button.','The app plays the same online game as the website: same accounts, same saves, same players. It always runs the newest version, and works offline too.','To sign in from the app, it opens your web browser for Google sign-in, then puts you back in the game.','Press F11 in the app for full screen.','The title screen and character creator no longer show a scrollbar on Windows.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-13',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Two-column menu',n:['The menu is laid out in two columns, so it\'s half as tall and everything fits on a phone screen without scrolling.','Keyboard and controller: up/down move between rows, left/right between the two columns.','"Save & quit to title" is now just "Save & quit" (it still saves and takes you to the title screen).']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-12',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Pets are items now',n:['There\'s a new PET slot on the equipment screen (P). The pet in it follows you; every other pet you own is an item in your bag.','Swap pets from your Bag (tap a pet, then Equip) or tap the PET slot on the equipment screen. Put away (unequip) sends your pet back to the bag.','Don\'t want a pet any more? Sell it at a shop, trade it at the World Market, or tap Release in your bag (tap twice).','New pets (bought from Marlo, or rare drops) go straight into your PET slot, and the pet they replace goes into your bag.','All the pets you already own are now in your bag, and the one following you stays in your PET slot.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-11',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Sign out fixed',n:['The Sign out and Switch Google account buttons in Options now work: they sign you out straight away and the screen updates to show you\'re signed out (Switch then opens Google\'s account picker).']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-10',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Switch accounts from Options',n:['Options now shows which Google account you\'re signed in as, with Sign out and Switch Google account buttons. Handy if several people play on one device: each Google account has its own character and save.','Not signed in? Options has a Sign in with Google button too.','Signing in to a different Google account on the same device now loads that account\'s own save (or starts a new character if it has none), instead of offering the other person\'s progress. The previous account\'s progress is saved to its account first.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-9',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'New quest log and quest tracking',n:['The Quests screen (Q) has been rebuilt. Every quest is in one place, from Elder Rowan, every village and island town, and the harbor voyages, under three tabs: Active, Available and Done. Tap a quest to see what it\'s about and its reward.','Track a quest: open it and tap Track this quest. New quests are tracked automatically when you start them.','The box under your health shows the tracked quest and its next step, like "Bring Elder Rowan 15 stone (6/15)", and tells you when it\'s on another island or inside a building.','A golden arrow next to your character points the way, with the distance: to the person to talk to, the nearest tree, rock or monster you need, the buoy to sail to or the harbor post to report to. When the spot is on screen, a marker bounces over it.','The map (M) circles the tracked spot too.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-8',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Plateaus, take two',n:['Plateau tops are much roomier: you can now walk right up to the cliff edges instead of being kept a full step back, so the narrow ridges in Ironcrest and No Man\'s Land are easy to get around.','Stairways are wider and run all the way down the cliff face to the ground, and there are more of them (Ironcrest, No Man\'s Land and Ashfall each have 40+).','Fewer trees and rocks clutter the tops, and they never block the way.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-7',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Paths up the plateaus',n:['You can now climb the big rock plateaus on Ironcrest, No Man\'s Land and Ashfall. Look for stone stairways cut into the cliffs, often right beside a trail.','The flat tops are yours to explore: Ironcrest\'s mountain spine has ore, rocks and pines up top, and the mesas of No Man\'s Land have rocks, ore and cacti. Rattlesnake Mesa can finally be climbed.','The cliff edges still block you, so take the stairs back down.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-6',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Sign-in fixes',n:['Fixed Google sign-in on phones, tablets and the Home Screen app: picking your account sometimes just dropped you back on the title screen. Sign-in now takes you to Google and straight back into the game, signed in, on every device.','If Google sign-in doesn\'t finish, the title screen now tells you why instead of quietly doing nothing.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-5',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Island bosses in the wiki',n:['The wiki\'s Bosses tab now lists all five island bosses (they were missing before), with their new pictures, where to find them, the shards that open their door and their rewards.','Each entry explains how the boss fights and what to watch for before each attack.','Every island boss has a 5% rare drop, listed in the wiki: the Webling pet (Briar Queen), the Warlord\'s blade (Iron Warlord), the Frostbite ring (Frost Wyrm), the Voidling pet (Void Herald) and the Outlaw\'s hat (Black Jack). They also appear under Pets and rare items.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-4',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Island bosses come to life',n:['The island bosses have been redrawn again, now with real animations: they walk, crawl, slither and drift toward you, and each attack has its own wind-up and strike.','Every attack now has a short tell before it lands. The Briar Queen rears up before spitting web, the Iron Warlord raises his greatsword before a sweep and lowers it before he charges, the Frost Wyrm rears back before it breathes ice, the Void Herald lifts its orbs before it casts, and Black Jack draws both pistols before he fires or lights dynamite over his head.','Watch for the wind-up: that\'s your moment to roll.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-3',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'New island boss art',n:['All five island bosses have been redrawn in the same style as the world bosses: the Briar Queen is a thorn-backed spider with a rose on her back, the Iron Warlord wears horned armour and a red cape, the Frost Wyrm rises from its coils, the Void Herald floats with a crown of shards, and Black Jack wears a long duster coat.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-2',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Island bosses',n:['The great sealed doors on every island now open, and each one hides an Island Boss: the Briar Queen (Whispering Ruins, Briarwood), the Iron Warlord (the Fallen Bastion, Ashfall), the Frost Wyrm (the Giant\'s Stair, Ironcrest), the Void Herald (the Fractured Temple, Shattered Expanse) and Black Jack, the Outlaw King (the Old Silver Mine, No Man\'s Land).','To open a door you need five sigil shards from that island. Its monsters drop them (about 1 in 25). The door glows once you have enough. Look at it to go in. Each fight uses five shards.','Island bosses fight with warning circles, shockwave rings, projectile fans, charges, leaps and summoned helpers, and they get faster at half health. Their health bar shows at the top of the screen.','Rare drops (5%): the Webling pet (Briar Queen), the Warlord\'s blade, the strongest sword in the game (Iron Warlord), the Frostbite ring, whose hits can freeze monsters (Frost Wyrm), the Voidling pet (Void Herald) and the Outlaw\'s hat (Black Jack). Every fight also pays out gold, bars and gems.','The wiki has an Island bosses section with pictures.']},
 {v:'2026.11.06-1',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:'Sailing and world map fixes',n:['Fixed: sailing straight between islands (Briarwood, No Man\'s Land and the Shattered Expanse) left your boat stuck at the edge of the map, in the wrong spot. You now arrive at the matching spot on the edge you sailed in from, and can sail away normally in both directions.','Fixed: the world map took a long time to draw the islands (especially on phones). The islands are now drawn in the background while you play, and much faster while the map is open.','The red buoy for the Lawless Waters voyage sits a little farther from the corner of the map, so you won\'t sail off the edge by accident while looking for it.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-24',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'The World Market, No Man\'s Land & new pets',n:['The World Market has opened just outside Hollow Village. Talk to the Market clerk (or hit the stalls) to put up offers to buy or sell anything with every player. Offers match automatically, even while you\'re offline, and what you get waits in your collection box at the market. Cancel any time to get back what hasn\'t traded. You need to be signed in.','New island: No Man\'s Land, a lawless desert south of Briarwood and west of the Shattered Expanse. PvP is always on there, for everyone. Look out for desert bandits (a "!" means they\'re aiming: roll!), Cacticus that pretend to be cacti, and giant scorpions. Explore Dustwater ghost town, Boot Hill, Rattlesnake Mesa and more.','To get there, take the new Lawless Waters voyage at the Tidewatch harbor post (after Into Briarwood). Once it\'s charted you can also sail off Briarwood\'s south edge or the Shattered Expanse\'s west edge.','You can now see your sword when you swing it: wooden, stone, iron, steel, the Crystal blade, mithril and adamant all look different, and other players see yours too.','More Foraging: mushroom patches grow beside trees (Foraging 5) and hazel bushes carry nuts (Foraging 10). Cacti now give real cactus fruit. Eat mushrooms and nuts raw, or roast them at a campfire.','New rare pet: the Squirrel (1 in 1,000 from berry bushes). It forages for you, bringing berries, nuts, mushrooms, cactus fruit, coins and sometimes a healing potion.','New rare pets: ore golems (1 in 2,000 from mining iron, gold, mithril or adamant ore). They stand around blinking, curl up and roll to keep up with you, and dig up their own ore for you.','The wiki is up to date: every dungeon (Thornroot Hollow, the Ironcrest mines and caves, Cinderdeep), boss and island monster, with pictures of the newer bosses and every pet, new guides, and the island towns.','Fixed: some rare drops and dungeons were missing from the wiki.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-23',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Hollow Island is twice as big',n:['Hollow Island has doubled in size. Hollow Village, Saltmere, Frosthollow, Dusthaven and Tidewatch are much farther apart, with more forest, snowfield and desert between them, and the roads stretch to match.','Your builds moved with the map: houses, castles, walls, chests, stations, beds, berry planters and farm plots are at the matching spot on the bigger island. Anything that would have landed in the water or on rock was packed into your bag, along with whatever was inside it.','The dungeons, the islets out at sea (Gull Rock, Wreck Isle, Hermit\'s Isle) and the Drowned Grotto moved out too.','Map markers stay easy to see on the bigger map.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-22',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Emberwatch, Cinderdeep & the Stone Sledgehammer',n:['Ashfall Coast has a forge camp: Emberwatch. Warden Kesh, Forgemaster Brann and Old Pell have four quests for you, Brann sells potions, iron arrows, bait and iron bars and buys anything, and monsters stay out of the camp.','New dungeon: Cinderdeep, six floors of ash and lava in Ashfall\'s north-east hills. Don\'t stand in the lava pools. At the bottom the Emberlord wakes once a day: it sets the ground under you on fire (watch the orange rings and roll out), throws fans of fireballs, and calls magma slimes at half health.','Rare drop from the Emberlord: the Ember ring. Your melee hits set monsters on fire.','New rare drop from the Stone Giant: the Stone Sledgehammer. Equip it in your main hand: it hits like an iron sword, and your ultimate (V, L1+R1, or the SLAM button) becomes a GROUND SLAM that hits everything around you. 18 second cooldown, no wand needed.','Boulders! Big boulders now sit on every island, and caves have them too. Break one with the Stone Sledgehammer for 35 to 50 stone. Ore boulders glint with iron, gold, mithril or adamant and give a big pile of ore (Mining 15 / 30 / 45 / 60).','Treelings for every tree: oak, willow, maple, yew, pine, Void Tree and dead-tree treelings, each 1 in 5,000 from chopping that kind of tree.','The purple-leaved trees of the Shattered Expanse are now called Void Trees.','You can walk into Thornbrook\'s Ranger Lodge and the Sleepy Fern inn (rest in a bed there to heal), and into Emberwatch\'s Forge and Warden\'s Hall.','Fixed: moss slimes looked like blue slimes. They\'re green now.','Fixed: killing briar wolves on Briarwood didn\'t count toward Ranger Wren\'s quest.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-21',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Thornbrook & Thornroot Hollow',n:['Briarwood Isle has a village: Thornbrook, with a ranger lodge, the Sleepy Fern inn and a market. Ranger Wren, Hazel the trader and Old Moss have four quests for you (see the Quests screen), Hazel sells potions, arrows, bait and seeds and buys anything, and monsters stay out of the village.','New dungeon: Thornroot Hollow, six floors under Briarwood\'s south-west roots. At the bottom waits the Thornheart, a huge walking tree that wakes once a day. Watch for the green rings: roots burst out of them. At half health it calls briar wolves.','Rare drop from the Thornheart: the Thorn amulet. Anything that hurts you takes 4 damage back.','Ironcrest\'s mines and caves are now six floors deep.','New furniture: the Trash can (Craft menu, Building). Put it in your house, then face it and press HIT to throw away things you don\'t want.','The cat, dog and fox pets have been redrawn to fit the game, and the anvil has a brand-new look.','Gates now keep monsters out. Only players can walk through them, on every island.','Trusted friends can now use your wardrobe.','Fixed: if a tree or rock grew back right where you were standing, you got stuck inside it. Now you\'re moved to the nearest open spot.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-20',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Dev tools',n:['Behind-the-scenes testing tools for the new castle and pets. Nothing changes for players.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-19',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'The islands update',n:['Fishing now works on every island, from the shore and from your boat, and each island has its own fish: pike and golden carp (Briarwood), ember eels and lava snappers (Ashfall), ice cod and glacier char (Ironcrest), void rays and crystal anglers (Shattered Expanse).','Farming is public: every tilled plot and crop belongs to everyone. Anyone can till, plant, water and harvest any plot on any island, and everybody sees the same fields growing.','Sail off the edge of the map! Once you have charted a route, sail into Hollow Island\'s west edge to reach Briarwood, east for Ashfall, north for Ironcrest and south for the Shattered Expanse. Sail back off the island\'s edge facing Hollow to come home.','Ironcrest Highlands has two mines and two caves (by the mining camps and in the cliffs). Three floors each, full of ore, and campfires work inside.','Far fewer monsters, and calmer ones: they only come for you when you get close or hit them, chase more slowly, and you get a little longer between hits.','Rain and snow now fall on the other islands too (ash haze on Ashfall), and rain waters crops there.','Every island\'s pier has a trader who buys what you gather.','Crystal veins now show the ore inside (gold, blue mithril, green adamant, lavender iron), and scorched or dark trees show what wood they give.','Rare pets: a wolf with a red collar (1 in 1,000 from each kind of wolf) and a little Treeling (1 in 5,000 trees chopped).','Sharks prowl the Shattered Expanse. They leave you alone, unless you\'re hurt and near the water.','New rare drop from the Stone Giant: a Castle. It works like a house, with a great hall inside, and its torches keep monsters away and heal you.','Fixed: ✕ on a controller now opens chests on the other islands.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-18',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Craft your own hoe',n:['You can now craft a hoe (3 wood, 2 stone) and a watering can (2 wood, 3 stone) in the Craft menu, under the tools. Both need Crafting 1. The general store still sells them too.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-17',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Controller landing fix, part 2',n:['Fixed: landing with ✕ on a controller on Briarwood, Ashfall, Ironcrest or the Shattered Expanse left you standing in the water next to the shore, unable to move. ✕ now puts you on land properly.','Landing is easier on rocky, jagged coasts and in narrow inlets: if there\'s land right beside the boat, you can go ashore there.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-16',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Controller landing fix',n:['Fixed: with a controller, pressing ✕ at the shore of Briarwood, Ashfall, Ironcrest or the Shattered Expanse swung your weapon instead of landing the boat, so you got stuck at the edge of the island. ✕ now lands and sets sail on every island.','✕ on a controller now also opens graves.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-15',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Find your grave',n:['When you fall, your grave now shows on your minimap and on the map (HERE and WORLD) as a little blinking tombstone, along with how long it has before it crumbles.','When your grave is on the same island as you, an arrow at the edge of the screen points the way and shows how far it is.','If you fell inside a building or a dungeon, the grave is marked at the door you went in by.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-14',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Open seas & new boats',n:['The sea now stretches on past the edge of the map. No more black void at the edge of Hollow Island.','Brand-new sailboats: a striped hull, a mainsail and a jib, and a little pennant that flaps in the wind. You now sit in the boat with your upper body showing, facing whichever way you sail.','You can now see other players sitting in their boats, with their names shown.','Boats tied up at the docks have their sails rolled up.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-13',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Farming tweak & Flame Aura',n:['Tilled soil with nothing planted in it turns back into grass after 10 minutes, on every island. Plant something to keep it.','Flame Aura (Firemaking 30) now really lights up the night around you while one of your campfires is burning, instead of just a faint orange tint.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-12',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Farming everywhere',n:['Farming now works on every island: till with your hoe, plant seeds from the Bag, water and harvest, just like on Hollow Island. Your crops on each island keep growing while you play, and other players can see your fields.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-11',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'New app icon',n:['The app icon is now your hero wearing the Flame Crown. On iPhone, remove the home screen icon and add it again (Share > Add to Home Screen) to see it.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-10',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'New app icon',n:['SkillQuest has a proper pixel-art icon: a crossed sword and pickaxe under a gold crown. On iPhone, remove the old home screen icon and add it again (Share > Add to Home Screen) to get it.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-9',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Fixes',n:['The Flame Crown\'s wisp is drawn on top, so fences and trees no longer hide it.','On phones, the world boss banner sits under your health and quest boxes instead of covering them.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-8',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Flame Crown fix',n:['Fixed: the flame wisp could be drawn far away from your campfire (often off-screen), so it looked like it never showed up. It now always appears at your fire.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-7',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Fixes',n:['Fixed: turning off Hide helmet could switch itself back on. It\'s now a button on the Equipment screen.','The title screen fits on phones again: Leaderboards, Wiki, Options and Report a bug sit two to a row, and the screen scrolls if it ever needs to.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-6',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Flame Crown fix',n:['Fixed: with the Lone Bonfire perk, lighting a new campfire made your flame wisp vanish instead of moving to the new fire.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-5',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'A bigger Wiki',n:['Skills: pick a skill to see just that one: how to train it, its perks and what it unlocks.','New wiki pages: Guides (getting a boat, unlocking the islands, making gold, world bosses, building a home, playing with friends), an XP table with a calculator, every Shop with prices, People (who\'s who and where), and Maps of every island with numbered landmarks.','Monsters and dungeon bosses now have pictures.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-4',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Patch notes',n:['Patch notes are now in the Wiki. The WIKI button shows NEW when there\'s an update you haven\'t read.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-3',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'The Wiki',n:['New: a Wiki on the title screen and in the START menu, with skills, items, crafting, monsters, bosses, dungeons, quests, islands and pets, plus search.','The Flame Crown now has proper side and back views.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-2',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Flame Crown',n:['New rare drop from the Flame Wisp: the Flame Crown. Wear it and your campfires call a little flame wisp that roams the fire\'s light and throws fireballs at monsters.']},
 {v:'2026.11.05-1',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:'Imp pet',n:['New rare drop from the Demon: an Imp pet with a poison dagger. It attacks whatever hurts you and comes back a minute after it falls.']},
 {v:'2026.11.04-4',d:'Nov 4, 2026',t:'One game per account',n:['Opening the game on a second device or tab now pauses the older one. Fixes players flickering and jumping around, trades failing, and two copies saving over each other.']},
 {v:'2026.11.04-3',d:'Nov 4, 2026',t:'Trusted friends',n:['Mark friends as TRUSTED (Chat > Friends) to let them use your stations, chests and beds, in your houses and at things you build outside. Chests are shared safely.','Visitors can no longer pick up (and copy) furniture in your house.','The game version is shown at the bottom of Options.']},
 {v:'2026.11.04-2',d:'Nov 4, 2026',t:'Dragonsoul & more',n:['New rare drop from the Ancient Dragon: the Dragonsoul Amulet. Your ultimate becomes Dragon Form: hold attack to breathe fire for 2 minutes.','PS4 controllers work in more browsers, and the Share button is named properly.','Options: a Fullscreen button (on iPhone, use Add to Home Screen).','Equipment: a Hide helmet option.']},
 {v:'2026.11.04-1',d:'Nov 4, 2026',t:'World bosses',n:['World bosses: the Flame Wisp, Stone Giant, Demon and Ancient Dragon appear every 30 minutes. Fight them together, dodge their telegraphed attacks and earn loot by damage rank.','All bosses redrawn in chunky pixel art, and they turn to face you.','Houses on any island; friends can visit them.','Leaderboards on the title screen. Sail around the other islands.','Firemaking perks: Lone Bonfire, Flame Aura and Hearthkeeper.','Ignore and report players from chat. Mithril and adamant bows and wands.','Fixes: bug reports with screenshots, names turning into "Adventurer", monsters standing on top of you, invisible campfires on other islands, and exit doors at the end of every dungeon.']},
 {v:'2026.11.03',d:'Nov 3, 2026',t:'Playing together',n:['Trading, public gravestones (your items wait 15 minutes where you fell), and opt-in PvP with safe zones.','See other players\' swings, arrows, spells and ultimates.','Build and cook on every island. Gold jewelry with gems. Marlo\'s Emporium: pets, capes, dyes, fine furniture and potions.','A shared world: one clock, shared trees, rocks, monsters, dungeons and campfires. Friends, private messages and friend requests.','Visit friends\' houses; see each other\'s farms, builds and boats.','A title screen, controller support, mouse and touch aiming, and a bug report button.']},
 {v:'2026.11.02',d:'Nov 2, 2026',t:'Online!',n:['SkillQuest goes online: Google sign-in, saves on your account, other players and chat.','OG crowns for everyone who signs in before Dec 3, 2026.']}];
window.SQVER=PATCH_NOTES[0].v;
